+| `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_SWIPE_TIMEOUT`                | (Optional) The timeout in ms before a swipe gesture is detected.                                                                 | `1000`              |
+| `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_SWIPE_DISTANCE`               | (Optional) Minimum move distance required for a swipe to be detected.                                                            | `500`               |
+| `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_SWIPE_THRESHOLD`              | (Optional) Movements in the alternate axis must be less than this threshold for a swipe to be detected.                          | `300`               |
+| `DIGITIZER_SWIPE_LEFT_KC`                      | (Optional) The keycode to generate when the fingers swipe left. 16-bit keycodes such as `C(KC_RIGHT)` are supported.             | `QK_MOUSE_BUTTON_3` |
+| `DIGITIZER_SWIPE_RIGHT_KC`                     | (Optional) The keycode to generate when the fingers swipe right. 16-bit keycodes such as `C(KC_LEFT)` are supported.             | `QK_MOUSE_BUTTON_4` |
+| `DIGITIZER_SWIPE_UP_KC`                        | (Optional) The keycode to generate when the fingers swipe up. 16-bit keycodes such as `C(KC_UP)` are supported.                  | `KC_LEFT_GUI`       |
+| `DIGITIZER_SWIPE_DOWN_KC`                      | (Optional) The keycode to generate when the fingers swipe down. 16-bit keycodes such as `C(KC_DOWN)` are supported.              | `KC_ESC`            |
+
+Swipe keycodes are sent with `tap_code16()`, so modified keycodes work. For example, to switch macOS desktops the way a native trackpad does:
+
+```c
+#define DIGITIZER_SWIPE_LEFT_KC C(KC_RIGHT)  // Fingers left: next desktop on the right
+#define DIGITIZER_SWIPE_RIGHT_KC C(KC_LEFT)  // Fingers right: previous desktop on the left
+#define DIGITIZER_SWIPE_UP_KC C(KC_UP)       // Mission Control
+#define DIGITIZER_SWIPE_DOWN_KC C(KC_DOWN)   // App Exposé
+```
 
